WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.820
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.880
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.290
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.400
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.540
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.100
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.290
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.360
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.450
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.210
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.490
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.420
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:12.870
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:25.180
Takara Fansubs

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.880
<i>The day finally came when the Ice Queen's heart melted.</i>

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:39.520
<i>Holding Angeletta close, she promised to cure Angeletta.</i>

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:49.040
<i>Leaving Romeo with many memories, Angeletta left for far-away Paris.</i>

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.980
Episode 24:

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.980
The Hunted Siblings

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.070
<i>Winter had finally come to Milan.</i>

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:07.510
<i>One day amidst the encroaching cold, an event began to unfold...</i>

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.910
<i>...that would change Romeo's life forever.</i>

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:15.070
<i>Not realizing the extent of the courage he would soon need,</i>

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:20.940
<i>...Romeo's day began with the usual preparations for work.</i>

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:24.770
Brrr!

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.390
You think Angeletta's doing okay, Piccolo?

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.040
I'm sure she's doing great.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.790
They're here!

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.910
She's wearing a diamond necklace.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.080
I'm really looking forward to the fifteenth, one week from now.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.820
I wonder what's going on next week?

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:00.940
Hey!

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.040
Nikita!

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:06.870
As out of it as ever, I see. Don't you know?

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.930
Next week's the Grand Duke's nuptials ceremony.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.090
Nuptials ceremony!

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.080
Nuptials... You mean marriage?

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.680
Aristos 'n rich folks from all over the country are getting together.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:24.000
Yeah! All over.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.250
Even the King of Italy will be here.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.210
Right! Even the King.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.130
Today's the pre-celebration opera.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.420
The marquis! The viscount!

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.710
<i>Where've I seen her before?</i>

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.970
<i>Blue eyes... Blond hair...</i>

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:52.320
No, she couldn't be...

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:07.620
Well! Romeo.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.400
Oh, hi, Doctor Casella.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:15.050
Perfect timing. I wanted to give this book to Alfredo.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.120
He's been dying to read it.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.270
Great, I bet he'll be delighted!

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:24.440
Since winter began, he hasn't come by to borrow any books. I'm wondering about him.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.560
I haven't seen much of him these days either.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.760
I think his padrone's pretty tough on him...

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:32.760
I'm kind of worried.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.120
Wine!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.250
I'm telling you to go buy me more wine.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.530
Alfredo! You listening?

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.020
I said go buy some wine!

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:03.780
We don't have money for that. We don't have enough to buy potatoes for dinner!

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.040
You spent all the money on liquor!

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:09.530
What's with that look?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.200
Don't you look down your nose at me.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.810
If we don't have money, then YOU'LL go without dinner.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.880
I haven't eaten in two days.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.470
Perfect.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:35.080
I'm going out.
Go and earn some money!

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.990
Gambling again...

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.740
Five lira. Got it?
- Five lira?!

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.070
Got it?

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:45.770
I'll be back tomorrow morning.
You'd better have it!

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:56.750
<i>Be as violent with me as you want.</i>

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:01.270
<i>You'll never crush my pride.</i>

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.750
Bianca.

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:30.210
<i>I must be tired.
I'm not acting like myself.</i>

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:34.370
Alfredo. Alfredo!

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.050
Ah, Alfredo!

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:41.950
Romeo.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.070
I brought you something nice.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.550
Finally, I can read another book.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.360
How many days has it been...

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:08.840
Alfredo... You really want to read more, don't you?

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:10.850
Yes, I do.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:12.860
And...

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:22.860
And study lots of things.
I want to gain more knowledge.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.230
Hey, hold up!

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:40.300
It's so unfair. Those boys get to read all the books they want.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:44.880
They get to study. If only you had the chance, too.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:47.840
It's OK. So long as you have the passion,

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:52.270
...hardships won't stand in the way of your dreams.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:53.610
Dreams?

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.280
You know, Romeo,

00:07:56.570 --> 00:08:00.640
...we Black Brothers have been sold off by adults, and made to suffer.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:05.160
There are many other children in the world like us.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:12.770
But there will come an age when we can all learn freely and live free.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:16.820
Learn freely... and live free?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:21.270
Yes... and we'll create that age!

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:31.900
So that's your dream, is it, Alfredo?

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:32.870
Yes.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:37.520
I know you'll be able to fulfill it one day.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:38.820
I won't be able to do it alone.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.300
Will you help me?

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:45.320
I... I wouldn't know what to do...

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:49.510
You've got to be with me!

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.510
All right!

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:01.920
All right!

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.020
We'll fulfill our dreams, together!

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:12.850
<i>Romeo never forgot the promise he and Alfredo made that day...</i>

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:18.210
<i>...a promise which was never to be fulfilled.</i>

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:22.640
<i>Indeed, despite their fervent vows of friendship,</i>

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.680
<i>...the wheels of fate were already in motion.</i>

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.760
How long are you going to make me wait?

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:41.730
I'm freezing to death without the stove.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.920
We've called a chimney sweep and he should be here any moment.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:50.060
If Madame would like, I can have another room prepared.

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:54.770
I've taken a liking to this room.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:10:00.000
We Martinis are on intimate terms with the King of Italy.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.410
What do you think he would say if we told him...

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:07.650
about this little mishap at next week's dinner party?

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:12.910
Please, don't be hasty.
I'll do something about...

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.200
Stop that racket!

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:25.570
That was on purpose, wasn't it? I know what you're up to.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:32.000
Perhaps a drink for the young lady?

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:37.090
No. Give her an inch and she'll take a mile.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:40.620
This the place with the clogged chimney?

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.760
Ah, here they are.

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:46.570
That's the chimney. Please fix it quickly.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:48.780
No problem.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:55.260
Stop! I told you to stop playing!

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:03.680
Hey. Romeo. Hurry up.
- Yessir.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:10.310
That kid rubs me the wrong way. I can't wait to get rid of her.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:17.700
Just be patient, and eventually she'll tell us where Alfredo is.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.120
Hey you!

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.210
Wait!

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.460
Grab hold of my hand.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:45.420
Leave me alone! Don't interfere!

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:48.970
Then I'm calling your father and mother...
- No, don't!!

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:52.700
Those two aren't my parents!

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:55.360
If you call them I'll jump!

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:13.440
Here, grab hold!

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:19.130
Wait! I'll help you.

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:25.670
Keep still. I'm coming.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:26.990
Stay away!

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:30.230
Please... Stay away!

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:36.120
Don't move!

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:38.100
You shouldn't move.

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:39.430
Stay away!

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:43.940
Watch out!

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:52.120
Stop it! Don't look down!

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:58.670
Quick. Grab the pipe!

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:04.690
Good...

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.630
Grab hold of me, tight.

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:08.210
Hurry!

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:18.860
Are you hurt?

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:25.560
Why'd you save me?! I know you were hired by those two to kill me.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:28.840
Me?! I was just trying to help you.

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:30.650
I don't know anything about...
- Liar!

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:34.270
I'm not a liar.
- Ouch. Let go!

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:36.510
Sorry.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:41.320
I don't know what's going on.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.660
I've never met a girl like you before.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.170
Wait!

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:48.420
Who are you?

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.090
Romeo.

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.030
A chimney sweep.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:54.150
A chimney sweep?

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:58.200
You wouldn't happen to be a friend of my brother?

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.560
The girl's gone. She got away!

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:04.790
Mauricio!

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:09.400
Over here, quickly. Catch Bianca!

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:12.570
Bianca? Did you say Bianca?

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:19.230
Hey you! Are you... are you Alfredo's little sister?

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:26.200
Remember, don't let her escape!

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.670
I have to tell Alfredo.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.750
What? Bianca?

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:41.620
Bianca.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.640
Let's go. We have to look for her. Hurry!

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.710
Bianca! Bianca!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.060
Where are you? Bianca!

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:56.240
Bianca!

00:14:57.430 --> 00:15:01.950
Bianca! Don't run away!

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:14.550
Bianca.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.490
Have you found Bianca yet?

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:20.680
Afraid not... 
- What are you doing, then!?

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.360
Hurry up and find her.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.760
You know that man, don't you?

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.090
Alfredo!

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:40.540
Looks like my anemia is acting up again...

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.090
Are you going to be okay?

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.600
I just need to rest a bit.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.570
Romeo.

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:53.590
It looks like it's finally time to tell you my secret.

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:55.590
Your secret?

00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:00.200
Do you remember the night by the lake, when we spoke together?

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:03.360
Sure I do. You talked about you and your sister.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:10.010
We're actually the children of Viscount Piedmont of the Martini's.

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:19.620
Bianca and I grew up in peace in the Martini mansion...

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:22.180
Until one year ago.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:30.180
Father and Mother were the most loving parents anyone could want.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:34.500
We were the picture of the happy family.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:40.160
But there were those who wished to destroy that happiness.

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:45.450
My father's younger brother Mauricio and his wife Grazela.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:50.480
Why does my brother get all the wealth and glory?

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:53.630
Just because he's the eldest son of the Martinis.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:57.970
So take it from him, Mauricio. Every last cent.

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:00.510
It's simple.

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:04.700
We just get rid of him.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:11.180
We told our parents what they'd said. But...

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:15.370
It couldn't be. Mauricio would never do such a thing.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:20.990
You must have misheard, Alfredo. Try not to worry about it.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:24.560
Be more trusting of them.
- But...

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:28.770
...catastrophe struck.

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:32.710
Alfredo! Bianca!

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.210
Father!

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:38.180
We've been betrayed.
Take this and get away!

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.130
It's the Martini household heirloom.

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:47.170
So long as that treasure exists, my pride and honor will be safely in your hands.

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:51.140
It's too late for us. Get away from here, Alfredo, Bianca!

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:55.550
Father! Mother!

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:01.150
The kids have escaped with the Martini treasure! Catch them!

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:07.960
We ran...

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.620
Eating little or nothing for days...

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:12.700
...with no one to aid us.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.270
They say we started the fire.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.520
We're wanted!

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.770
Those two are after this.

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:39.410
They'll be chasing us.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.390
Big brother...

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.520
I won't let them catch us.

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:48.230
If it's the last thing I'll do, I'll protect you and Father's treasure.

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:54.880
I cut Bianca's long hair.

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:58.190
Bianca told me to.

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:01.190
She said it would throw them off the scent.

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:07.250
And a month later we stumbled across a farm village.

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:11.720
Bianca was so tired she couldn't walk anymore.

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:20.080
Where are you two coming from?

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:25.830
Goodness, you two were starving. 
- And all decked out in your Sunday best.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:30.920
Really. I've never seen such an expensive-looking dress.

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:35.220
Please let us stay here a while.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:38.860
We can help you cut grass, tend the animals, anything.

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:41.900
And I'll work with my brother.

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:44.790
I don't know...

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:51.800
It was then that the God of Death, Luini, appeared in that village.

00:19:55.390 --> 00:20:01.740
I decided to go to Milan and become a chimney sweep to protect Bianca.

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:07.420
I gave the payment to the farmers to cover the cost of raising Bianca.

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:14.940
Finally, it was time for Bianca and I to go our separate ways.

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:20.180
No! I don't want you to leave, big brother!

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:26.690
It's the only way we'll survive, Bianca.

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:28.960
I'll come find you soon, I promise.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:33.500
Until then, whatever you do, don't let yourself get caught.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.160
Big brother!

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:46.830
Bianca!

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:49.210
Big brother!

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:59.460
Soon after that, Bianca must have been caught by Mauricio.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.110
Then they took her to Milan.

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:04.780
So that's it.

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:09.140
If only I'd stayed, this would never have happened!

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:12.640
Alfredo...

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:14.960
Let's rescue your sister.

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:16.790
Let's go look for her.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.010
Romeo.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:32.790
Alfredo must be in this city.

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:37.200
Alfredo, where are you?
- Bianca.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:43.220
I thought I told you... You'll never escape.

00:21:56.510 --> 00:21:58.890
<i>Bianca was recaptured.</i>

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:02.610
<i>But it's Alfredo that Mauricio was really after.</i>

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:07.370
<i>Alfredo, I promise you we'll rescue Bianca!</i>

00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:12.580
See you then!

00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:12.580
<i>The Reunion of Bianca and Alfredo</i>

00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:12.580
Next time:

00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:18.070
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:26.680 --> 00:22:30.780
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:30.880 --> 00:22:35.080
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:39.280
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:43.480
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:48.390
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:48.390 --> 00:22:52.290
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:52.690 --> 00:22:59.590
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:01.290 --> 00:23:05.190
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:05.390 --> 00:23:09.390
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
